T["Observe memory for ten minutes without changing polling or forcing garbage collection. /rm perf memory accepts 1–1800 seconds (default 600), plus stop and report. Whole-Lua heap is sampled each second; bounded retained counts every thirty seconds. Addon attribution refreshes only at start and completion; intermediate values are cached with unknown age. Stop completes the final boundary before you open the report. Refreshes can hitch, and their cost is reported. Heap decreases do not prove collection or a leak."] = 2397
-- 65848052
T["Open the copyable lifetime report: whole-heap range and decreases, start/end addon attribution, explicitly cached intermediate values, retained key/row counts and capture overhead. Counts are not bytes; unavailable and capped observations stay explicit. Viewing the report never resamples memory."] = 2398
-- 35fde7b4
T["Measure normal rotation evaluation calls for ten seconds with the native profiler. /rm perf runtime accepts 1–60 seconds (default 10), plus stop and report. The 512-dispatch safety limit can end a longer capture sooner. Polling stays unchanged. Stop finalizes partial measurements; the legacy Cancel capture action still cancels. Close configuration after starting. Instrumentation adds overhead; allocation is not retained memory or proof of a leak. Cumulative CPU captures cannot overlap this capture."] = 2399
-- b429fad0
T["Open the copyable runtime report: measured evaluation calls, native elapsed time and gross allocation/deallocation counters. Missing metrics remain unavailable. Measurement covers evaluation calls only, not all addon events or rendering. Reading the report does not sample gameplay."] = 2400
-- 0eebb1cd
-- Context: Help topic title (General settings help) for the option in the performance section that
--     turns the observation cache on or off.
T["Enable observation cache"] = 2401
-- 5309abf9
T["Optional reuse of repeated getCached and getRetryCached lookups. Observation caching is off by default to reduce table allocations; enabling it can help conditions that repeat the same lookup. Compiled condition facts are independent of this option. The checkbox shows the saved choice for the next reload. Pending means it differs from the running mode. Use /reload to apply it; no full game restart is needed. This choice saves immediately without applying or discarding other pending settings."] = 2402
-- e2747e8f
T["Capture native cumulative function CPU costs and call counts for ten seconds. /rm perf cpu starts the same capture; /rm perf cpu 30 chooses 30 seconds (range 1–60). /rm perf cpu stop finalizes partial counters; /rm perf cpu report opens the copyable result. Capture uses live settings and does not apply pending changes. Close configuration after starting. WoW scriptProfile must already be enabled before a reload; RM never changes it or resets shared counters. Profiling itself adds overhead."] = 2403
-- 144f6416
T["Open a selectable, copyable report with total addon CPU, measured function costs and calls, sample boundaries, and unavailable or replaced functions. Inclusive costs overlap and must not be added together. Boundary state does not prove configuration or combat stayed unchanged throughout the capture. Untracked functions and native work may account for remaining costs."] = 2404
-- 8c53a218
T["Choose a source helper and its name in this Lua body, such as custom.ready or utils.getCached. These are dependency records even when the source and local names match; a different local name is an optional alias. The records identify helpers for loading, export and availability checks. Accepting a completion records the dependency automatically. Typing a call does not infer a dependency: add its qualified name explicitly or accept a completion. WoW globals and existing addon APIs remain directly available. Namespaces are private to this callback and do not supply self. Pass a method receiver explicitly in a namespaced dot call; object:method(x) is shorthand for object.method(object, x). Click the bound source name to open its function; the adjacent arrow changes the mapping. Pending edits offer Apply, Discard or Cancel before navigation. Renaming a function, namespace or binding does not rewrite code. Missing, disabled or invalid dependencies keep consumers unavailable."] = 2405
