T["Write to your own chat frame. Other players do not receive this message."] = 2516
-- 2224d247
T["Enter the message for a chat destination. The substitutions below insert action and cast information when it is available. This text is not used for Audible or named Emote output."] = 2517
-- 5625f190
T["For cast entries, {{spell}} is a spell link, {{item}} an item link and {{event}} the localized event name. {{target}} uses the recorded cast target, with the last recorded target for that spell as a fallback; it does not automatically use your selected target or your name. Unavailable cast substitutions can remain unchanged. Via Script/Macro instead uses its supplied target and spell, {{event}} becomes Via Script/Macro, and required missing inputs skip output; this API supplies no {{item}}."] = 2518
-- a7af0c5c
T["Choose a sound supplied by the shared-media catalog, then click Play to preview it. Preview is local and does not save the draft. An unavailable sound cannot be previewed; Audible announcements require a nonempty sound selection."] = 2519
-- 58fc69dd
T["The pill turns this entry on or off while keeping its fields. Disabled entries do not announce matching casts or macro invocations. Apply saves the changed state."] = 2520
-- 2ca49225
T["Edits stay in a draft until Apply. Complete the action or Via Script/Macro identifier and other required fields before saving. Discard abandons changes to saved announcements; Cancel closes a new creation draft. Leaving pending changes offers Apply, Discard or Cancel navigation."] = 2521
-- af92b7de
T["Use the sidebar buttons to create, duplicate, transfer or compare announcements. Apply saves the imported draft; Compare does not merge entries. Via Script/Macro Duplicate assigns a distinct identifier and every copied output gets a fresh identity. Series exports use version 2; version 1 remains available for legacy single-output entries. Imports and Apply reject ambiguous identifiers. The red trash permanently deletes the selected saved entry after confirmation. Resolve pending edits first; deletion does not carry into the next selected draft."] = 2522
-- 2aefc10f
T["An item set is an ordered list of alternatives, such as different mana potions. Runtime selection checks the list from the top for a carried or, where requested, equipped item. Priority comes from the order you choose, not the item level. Selecting an item does not by itself prove that it is usable, off cooldown, or in range; action readiness is checked separately."] = 2523
-- f684e8a2
T["Name the selected set so it can be found in the sidebar and referenced by rotations or conditions. New opens a name form; its first Apply saves an empty named set. Add items afterward and Apply again to save them. Discarding later item edits keeps that already saved set. Renaming a set does not change its identity in saved references."] = 2524
-- 21312192
T["Checked stores this set in the shared global collection, available to other profiles and characters using this addon database. Unchecked stores it in the current profile, which can itself be shared by characters. This is a staged move; Apply saves it. A profile set takes precedence if a global set has the same saved identity."] = 2525
-- 0ba4e811
T["The list of item cards is the priority order. Put preferred items first. RM can leave a selection unavailable when required inventory or identity observations are missing; it does not treat unknown data as proof that a lower-priority item should be used. The sidebar icon represents the first defined item and need not be the currently carried or highlighted one."] = 2526
-- a5bf7ef1
T["Search by item name and choose a result, or drag an item from your bags or action bar into its field. The icon identifies the item; metadata can take time to load. Edit a row to replace that entry. Use its red trash can to remove it rather than clearing a required item field."] = 2527
-- 67b1eae9
T["Choose or drag an item into the empty item field above the list, then click Add item to append it to the priority list, or drag Add item into a gap between cards to insert it there. Entering an item in this field alone does not add a row."] = 2528
-- 50b0f89c
T["Move Up / Move Down"] = 2529
-- 69b751c9
T["Use the arrows on the left, or drag an item row into a highlighted insertion gap. Ctrl-drag moves that row and all following entries together. The floating preview identifies what you are moving. Moves past the beginning or end are unavailable. Reordering changes priority and stays in the draft until Apply."] = 2530
-- 2b906316
-- Context: Help topic title in the item set help for the buttons that connect an item set to a
--     macro/action button or remove the link.
T["Bind / Unbind"] = 2531
-- 81abb5f4
T["Outside combat, apply pending item-set edits before binding. Drag the set (its row in the list, or the Bind pill) onto any action bar slot; an occupied slot swaps, leaving its previous action on the cursor. Or click Bind and then click an empty slot. Both pick up the first available item of the set. RM records the slot and updates it as item availability changes. The pill shows bound slot numbers; click it to unbind and remove still-matching bar items. Replaced bar actions are preserved. Binding changes are immediate action-bar operations, independent of the draft and its history."] = 2532
-- 7c8417f1
T["Restore the packaged item list for this set. Reset is available only for a set with a packaged default. The restored list is staged until Apply; the name is kept."] = 2533
-- 70b9c94e
T["The red trash can at the top right permanently removes the selected saved set after confirmation. Resolve pending edits before the final warning. References in rotations or conditions then need another set. Deletion reconciles still-matching bound bar actions and keeps the set if unbinding fails; the next selection opens without an unsaved deletion marker."] = 2534
-- 49c1588e
-- Context: Help topic title in the item set help for the undo and redo buttons.
T["Undo / Redo"] = 2535
-- cd68dbfd
T["Undo and Redo travel through recent item-set draft edits, including replacements, additions, ordering and row removals. They are unavailable when that direction has no history. Apply, Discard or leaving the page clears this bounded history. They do not reverse confirmed entity deletion or explicit action-bar binding operations."] = 2536
-- 68ab50bb
T["Ordinary item-set edits stay in a draft until Apply. Discard restores the saved item sets. Cancel closes a new creation draft. Leaving with pending changes offers Apply, Discard or Cancel navigation. Invalid fields must be corrected before Apply; Discard can abandon them."] = 2537
-- b81b94df
T["Use the buttons below the sidebar to create, duplicate, transfer, or compare sets. Duplicate makes an independent profile copy. Import shows the source name and can create a renamed copy or replace the selected list; Apply saves the staged result. Compare inspects differences without merging or modifying either set."] = 2538
-- 147db4bf
-- Context: Help topic title in the item set help: older macro buttons made before the current
--     system.
T["Legacy macro buttons"] = 2539
-- 77908784
T["Legacy clients may allow /click to invoke an RM item-set button separately from action-bar binding. The name is RM_ followed by the set name with non-alphanumeric characters removed, then an underscore and unit token. For a set named Bandages, an example is /click [@mouseover,nodead,help] RM_Bandages_mouseover. Other unit suffixes include player, pet, target, focus, pettarget, targettarget, focustarget, and mouseovertarget. These buttons contain item-use macro lines and do not provide the same readiness or first-item guarantee as the recommendation engine. Availability is subject to the client's secure-button and macro restrictions; reference-only support does not promise executable macro buttons."] = 2540
-- 0378c27f
T["Search for an item or drag it into the item field or icon. Choose the result to retain its exact item identity. The icon and name may be unavailable until metadata loads. Field clearing and save behavior belong to the editor that contains this list; use Delete when you intend to remove an entry."] = 2541
-- 6a348c09
T["Move this entry to the first position in the item priority list, when that control is offered."] = 2542
-- 3b1a1705
T["Move this entry one position earlier. A move before the first entry is unavailable."] = 2543
-- a147318d
T["Move this entry one position later. A move past the final entry is unavailable."] = 2544
-- 4b77e29f
T["Move this entry to the final position in the item priority list, when that control is offered."] = 2545
-- 0c112c0c
T["Remove this entry from the list. In a draft editor this remains pending until Apply, and Discard abandons the row edit. Undo is available where the containing editor provides draft history. This differs from permanently deleting the entire set after confirmation."] = 2546
-- df1955d5
T["Use All, Built In or Custom to choose the condition source, then filter by Switch, Other or a named category. Search above these controls narrows the visible list without changing assignments."] = 2547
-- 190e427d
T["Open Manage categories below the list for category maintenance. Manage conditions returns to individual condition settings."] = 2548
-- a9dcdfe2
T["Below the condition list, Import/Export opens the selected custom definition for transfer and code review; it is disabled for built-in conditions. In Manage categories, transfer a category’s ordered condition identifiers. Named categories and Other are exclusive destinations. Switch membership is independent."] = 2549
-- 936a161c
-- Context: Help topic title in Integrations settings help for the Lua editor options.
T["Editor"] = 2550
-- 0c601351
-- Context: Help topic title in Integrations help: the list of other addons Rotation Master can work
--     with.
T["Optional addons"] = 2551
-- 0413ac9a
T["Undo and Redo edit the Lua body. Reset restores the saved body or new-function template and can be undone. Check syntax executes no custom Lua. Apply saves the body and metadata together; Discard abandons the draft. Leaving with changes offers Apply, Discard or Cancel."] = 2552
-- 5e86a29a
T["Include custom function dependencies exports their source with the selected definition. Without it, the bundle records required helper identities and versions. Review source shows every imported Lua body. Resolve each original name and destination with Reuse, Replace or a new identifier. Apply import saves the complete reviewed bundle and can register imported Lua. Only apply code you trust."] = 2553
-- b696d1d1
-- Context: Section title in the Functions help: how the Arguments and Returns lists work.
T["Arguments and returns"] = 2554
-- 2be54423
T["Choose an existing namespace from the suggestions or type a new dotted namespace. Built In namespaces follow source files; custom namespaces are implied by saved functions and need no separate maintenance."] = 2555
-- f6a949d3
T["Function names use letters, numbers and underscores, beginning with a letter or underscore. The code signature shows the qualified namespace.name used by callers."] = 2556
-- 330af7d6
T["Search helpers by name or description, then filter Built In / Custom and namespace. Packaged helpers use the same read-only pane. Duplicate creates an editable custom copy."] = 2557
-- e67ec7ba
T["Click an Arguments or Returns heading to collapse or expand it. + Argument and + Return append when clicked, or insert at a highlighted gap when dragged. Drag a row or use Up / Down to reorder; Ctrl-drag carries following rows. The trash can removes a row. Type and Nullable document accepted values; Description explains each input or result. Lua can return several ordered results. Return rows describe those results; moving them does not rewrite return statements. Reordering a saved function warns because positional callers may need changes; RM does not rewrite call sites."] = 2558
-- 183f4958
T["Enable Rotation Master recommendations, automatic rotation switching and bound item-set updates. Disabling clears active advice and highlights and hides the preview. Apply saves the change."] = 2559
-- c25b80af
T["Set how often Rotation Master reevaluates the active rotation and independent cooldowns, in seconds. A shorter interval updates advice more often and uses more processing time. It does not cast spells, queue actions, or predict future combat."] = 2560
-- 693c25ac
T["Out of combat with no target and no focus, Rotation Master skips a polling tick unless something it watches has changed: auras, cooldowns, health or power of you, your pet or party, movement, casting, equipment, bags, form, pets or group. It still re-checks at least this often, for time-based conditions (aura or cooldown remaining), distance, and custom code. In combat, with any target or focus, or while configuration is open, every polling tick is evaluated. Zero evaluates every polling tick."] = 2561
-- 658535de
T["With automatic switching, Rotation Master checks this often, in and out of combat, whether a different rotation's switch conditions now match, so conditions that change on their own (nearby enemy count, threat, movement, health) take effect. Target, focus and pet changes are checked straight away. Zero turns automatic switching off. Choosing a rotation manually still overrides automatic switching until you choose Auto again."] = 2562
-- 93a9cab7
T["Hide the main rotation recommendation on action bars. Independent cooldown highlights remain available. Enable Preview Spells if you want to see the main advice in a separate window; with both displays off, the main recommendation has no visible icon."] = 2563
-- 186fa30f
T["How often, in seconds, the rotation editor checks each card's condition for the colored bar on the left of its condition field: green when it currently matches for you, red when it does not, gray when it cannot be read at the moment (hover the condition for why and when it was checked). Conditions are checked only while the editor is open; zero turns the bars off. This is separate from the recommendation polling interval."] = 2564
-- 8fc06fca
T["Show the Rotation Master minimap icon. Left-click toggles the configuration window. Right-click opens the quick menu for enabling recommendations and choosing a rotation or automatic switching."] = 2565
-- a64c178e
T["Choose how many seconds of previous spell casts to retain for history-based conditions. Older casts are removed as recommendations update. A longer history retains more records."] = 2566
-- 6572d0ab
T["Choose how many seconds of combat events to retain for conditions such as recent hits, parries and blocks. Older events are removed as recommendations update. Availability depends on the client combat-data policy."] = 2567
-- 6c970b96
T["Choose how many seconds of observed damage and healing to retain for burn-rate and time-to-die estimates. Recent observations receive more weight. A longer window uses more records and smooths short changes; it cannot supply events the client does not expose."] = 2568
-- 1826b95e
T["Choose a whole number of upcoming recommendations, from zero (hidden) to five. This is the only switch for the preview window: it is shown whenever this is above zero and hidden at zero, and the window has no close button. The preview shows current priority results, not a simulation of future cooldowns or combat. Icons start at 64 pixels; resizing scales all icons while preserving their square shape and the window ratio."] = 2569
-- 9a03212a
T["Adjust the preview background opacity without fading its icons. At zero only the icons remain, the hidden background does not intercept blank-space clicks and the resize grip is unavailable; an unlocked preview can still be dragged by its icons. Restore opacity in General to resize it."] = 2570
-- 7884cae2
T["Unlocked, drag the preview by any icon or its background to move it, and resize it from the grip that appears at its lower-right corner on hover. Locked, it cannot be moved or resized and its background lets clicks through. Right-click an icon (or the background while unlocked) for a menu to lock, unlock or open these settings. Locking and unlocking take effect immediately and are saved without Apply. Other pending General edits remain unchanged."] = 2571
-- 110dd6c2
T["Arrange preview icons horizontally (default) or vertically. Lock, Direction and Reset share one row below the opacity slider. Changing direction keeps icons square and adjusts the window ratio."] = 2572
-- 46417b1b
T["This icon previews the selected profile effect, color, size, anchor and offsets. Previewing an effect does not save the draft or change the spell being recommended."] = 2573
-- 0e030acc
T["Choose the highlight used for the main recommendation and as the default for independent cooldowns. Manage available effects on the Effects page. A cooldown can override these profile settings in its action details."] = 2574
-- cf6729fa
T["Scale the highlight relative to its action icon. A value of 1 uses the icon size. Drag the slider or type its numeric value; the preview updates as you edit."] = 2575
-- 15842be8
T["Choose the highlight color and opacity. Click the color swatch to open the picker, or enter R, G, B and A values between 0 and 1. Alpha controls opacity; individual cooldowns may override this profile color."] = 2576
-- 27eafca9
T["Choose the point on the action icon where a texture highlight is anchored by its center. Changing Anchor resets the offsets. The preview shows the resulting placement; non-texture glows may use offsets without a texture anchor."] = 2577
-- 24139be0
T["Vertical offset in pixels. Use Up or Down on the position control, or edit V directly. Hold Shift while using an arrow for ten pixels. Center resets both offsets and the anchor to Center."] = 2578
-- 64fcca62
T["Horizontal offset in pixels. Use Left or Right on the position control, or edit H directly. Hold Shift while using an arrow for ten pixels. Non-texture glows interpret offsets according to their effect shape."] = 2579
-- 199fbfc5
T["Choose the display name for your primary specialization. This changes its label in Rotation Master, not your character talents or specialization."] = 2580
-- 1647f2ad
T["Choose the display name for your secondary specialization. This changes its label in Rotation Master, not your character talents or specialization."] = 2581
-- b49fc138
T["Choose the amount of Rotation Master chat output. Silent suppresses routine output. Default reports normal changes such as rotation switching. Debug adds runtime statistics and trigger information. Verbose includes detailed condition and highlight activity and can produce substantial output."] = 2582
-- d0d316d9
T["Include component timings in the periodic Debug or Verbose profiling report. Reports show measured runs, total, minimum, average and maximum in milliseconds. Timings include child work; nested scopes overlap and must not be added together. The overall scope starts after rotation preparation. This is elapsed timing, not the native addon CPU report."] = 2583
-- fd1963a1
T["Effects define how action-bar icons are highlighted. They are shared across characters. General settings select the main recommendation effect and cooldown default; individual cooldowns can choose another effect. Select an effect in the sidebar to inspect or edit it."] = 2584
-- 40b0b9e0
T["Give the effect a name used by selectors in General and cooldown action details. New drafts can change type and fields before being named, but Apply requires a nonempty, unique name."] = 2585
-- 5a00db51
T["Choose the highlight implementation. Changing type stages the new fields and resets its sequence because different sequence types store different values. Choosing the current type preserves existing values. Apply saves the change; Discard restores the saved effect."] = 2586
-- c228a709
T["Texture: overlay a single image from game data or an installed addon. Its color, magnification and position come from the profile or the individual cooldown."] = 2587
-- cd1a7948
T["Pixel: animate short lines around the action icon border. Lines, Frequency, Length and Thickness control this library glow."] = 2588
-- 8f767bf7
T["Auto Cast: animate groups of glowing particles around the action icon. Particles, Frequency and Scale control this library glow."] = 2589
-- 0984e57a
T["Glow: use the familiar Blizzard-style button glow. Frequency controls its animation rate."] = 2590
-- 4f13ce4d
T["Dazzle: keep one texture and cycle through the sequence of colors. Each sequence card contains one RGBA color."] = 2591
-- 518c7a0b
T["Animate: cycle through the sequence of texture images. Each card selects one image and previews that selection."] = 2592
-- 7db1adc9
T["Pulse: keep one texture and cycle through the sequence of magnifications. Each card selects one scale relative to the action icon."] = 2593
-- 04c25e44
T["Rotate: animate one texture through evenly spaced angles around a full circle. Steps chooses the number of angles and Reverse changes their order."] = 2594
-- e239b9d1
T["Custom: cycle through cards containing a texture, angle, magnification and color. Each card supplies its own settings instead of relying on one shared texture."] = 2595
-- 1b35109f
T["The image beside Name and Type previews the current draft with a white color and standard size. Texture and sequence changes update the preview without saving. Actual recommendations use their profile or cooldown color, size and offsets."] = 2596
-- 69030e6a
T["For Texture, Dazzle, Pulse and Rotate, choose the image used throughout the effect. The arrow beside an image field opens the bundled overlay catalog with previews. Enter an available texture path or numeric file ID to use another image. Animate and Custom choose images in their sequence cards using the same controls. Selections update the draft and preview; Apply saves them."] = 2597
-- 06895a3f
T["Pixel effects: choose the number of animated lines around the button, from 1 to 20."] = 2598
-- 5a02f176
T["Pixel effects: signed cycles per second. A larger magnitude moves faster; a negative value reverses direction. Zero uses the glow library default of one cycle every four seconds."] = 2599
-- 912f8432
T["Pixel effects: choose line length in pixels. The glow library limits it to the smaller button dimension."] = 2600
-- 888c1858
T["Pixel effects: choose line thickness in pixels, from 1 to 5."] = 2601
-- f169cd48
T["Auto Cast effects: choose 1 to 4 particles in each of the glow library particle groups."] = 2602
-- 439eb6b4
T["Auto Cast effects: signed cycles per second. A larger magnitude moves faster; a negative value reverses direction. Zero uses the glow library default of one cycle every eight seconds."] = 2603
-- ee4e74b2
T["Auto Cast effects: scale the particles relative to the glow library default. A value of 1 uses their normal size."] = 2604
-- 7a5e1fd3
T["Glow effects: adjust the library animation rate. Larger positive values animate faster. Zero uses the library default rather than stopping the glow."] = 2605
-- a09487cf
T["Dazzle effects: seconds between color cards. A smaller positive interval changes colors more often; the sequence repeats after the last color."] = 2606
-- 9e3ad582
T["Animate effects: seconds between texture cards. A smaller positive interval changes images more often; the sequence repeats after the last image."] = 2607
-- 73861ddb
T["Pulse effects: seconds between magnification cards. A smaller positive interval changes size more often; the sequence repeats after the last size."] = 2608
-- 6f691c60
T["Rotate effects: seconds between angle steps. A smaller positive interval rotates faster. One full cycle uses this interval multiplied by Steps."] = 2609
-- 78b58b96
T["Rotate effects: choose 2 to 36 evenly spaced angles for a full turn. More steps at the same Frequency interval make a longer complete cycle."] = 2610
-- 98768f9e
T["Rotate effects: reverse the order of angle steps. Changing this checkbox does not alter the texture or number of steps."] = 2611
-- 0eaebb24
T["Custom effects: seconds between sequence cards. A smaller positive interval changes settings more often; the sequence repeats after the last card."] = 2612
-- a85d837a
T["Sequence cards play in order and repeat. Add step, on the Sequence header row, appends a card; drag Add step into a gap to insert one there. Drag a card into an insertion gap to reorder it; hold Ctrl when starting to carry it and all following cards. Up and Down move one card and are disabled at their respective ends. The red trash removes a card from the draft. Canceling a drag restores its original position."] = 2613
-- d5a4691e
T["Animate and Custom cards: choose a texture path or numeric file ID. The card preview shows the selected image. Custom also keeps an independent angle, magnification and color on that card."] = 2614
-- e9c4d7cb
T["Custom cards: set the texture angle in degrees from 0 to 359. This is the angle for this card, rather than a continuous rotation speed."] = 2615
-- f9eb09ea
T["Pulse and Custom cards: scale the texture relative to the action icon. A value of 1 uses the icon size. Use the slider or edit its numeric value."] = 2616
-- a6ca83b6
T["Dazzle and Custom cards: choose an RGBA color. Click the swatch to open the picker, or edit channels between 0 and 1. Alpha controls opacity."] = 2617
-- d838f5ee
T["Edits and sequence changes remain in a draft. Apply saves; Discard restores the saved effect. Cancel closes a new creation draft. View Changes compares saved and unsaved values. New drafts require a unique name and valid fields before Apply. Leaving with edits offers Apply, Discard or Cancel."] = 2618
-- 781f5d06
T["The red trash at the upper right deletes the selected effect after a permanent-deletion warning. Resolve pending edits first. Choose a replacement for any profile or cooldown using that effect; deletion does not silently rewrite those references."] = 2619
-- a8f923ca
T["New, Duplicate, Import/Export and Compare are below the sidebar. Duplicate copies the selected effect into a draft. Transfers show the original name and let you create a renamed copy or replace the selection when allowed. Compare inspects differences without saving them."] = 2620
-- fe52fcf9
T["Selecting a sidebar row only inspects that profile. Activate profile switches the live profile immediately, including its rotations and settings. The active profile shows Active profile instead. This operation does not wait for page Apply."] = 2621
-- 605ecea0
T["Choose a source to replace the active profile after confirmation. This copies settings and rotations into the active profile, even when the sidebar is inspecting a different profile. It does not switch to the source or rename the active profile. Cancel at the confirmation preserves the current profile."] = 2622
-- d403202f
T["Reset current profile replaces the active profile with its defaults after confirmation. Custom rotations and settings in it are replaced. The control is disabled while inspecting another profile. Reset is immediate after confirmation; there is no later page Apply to undo it."] = 2623
-- 071e02f8
T["The red trash can permanently removes the selected inactive profile after confirmation. The active profile and Default cannot be deleted here. Selecting another profile does not delete or activate it."] = 2624
-- e0223ba4
T["New and Duplicate open a named draft. Use a nonblank, unused name of at most 50 characters. Apply creates the profile; Cancel abandons creation. Creating a profile leaves the previously active profile active, so use Activate profile when you want to switch to the new copy."] = 2625
-- c85ff72a
T["The buttons below the list create a new profile, duplicate the selected profile, transfer profiles or compare saved settings. Search narrows the list without activating a profile. Import/Export shows the original name and lets you replace the selection or create a renamed copy. Importing a new profile opens a creation draft; Apply saves it. Replacing a selected profile happens when you confirm the import, and replacing the active profile updates its runtime settings. Compare does not apply changes."] = 2626
-- d58adae2
T["Status pills show Not loaded, Supported, Disabled, Enabled or Selected. Click Enabled to Select or Disable. Disabling Selected chooses the sole enabled available editor, offers a choice when several exist, or leaves none selected. Enabling an editor when none is selected selects it automatically. Native is always available; its Syntax highlighting option is independent of editor selection. With no enabled editor, emergency plain text remains usable. Apply saves preferences for the next source-editor opening; Discard keeps saved settings. An open editor keeps its current provider."] = 2627
-- 3bdeb012
T["Show line numbers controls the gutter in every condition and function code editor. It defaults to enabled. Apply saves the preference and updates open code panes; Discard keeps the saved setting. It does not change the Lua source or its line breaks."] = 2628
-- e69d5940
T["Addon names open copyable official release and source links across available providers. Edition filtering follows declared support for the matching addon identity; unknown compatibility remains visible. An older release date alone does not prove incompatibility. Listed game-edition support describes publisher release evidence, not certification of the integration on your client. Some integrations have only historical or unverified releases. Not loaded means unavailable to RM; Supported identifies an available integration without an enable switch. Bundled libraries are excluded. Rotation Master does not install or enable other addons."] = 2629
-- 6c182d42
-- Context: Help topic title for the buttons that save or abandon edits in an item list dialog and
--     the window.
T["Apply / Discard"] = 2630
-- d04a65ba
T["Edits stay in a draft until Apply. Discard abandons pending changes. Leaving with changes offers Apply, Discard or Cancel; Cancel keeps the page and draft open. Effect previews do not save changes. Action-bar binding operations are explicit and immediate."] = 2631
-- 2be8c485
T["Diagram / List changes only the rotation view; General settings choose the default. Diagram has floating minus, percentage and plus controls at the bottom right. Scroll to zoom from 25% to 200%; click the percentage or middle-click to reset to 100%. Drag empty diagram space to pan. List uses normal scrollbars with touching cards and boxed branch arms, False before True. Cooldowns use a separate scrolling grid. Dragging cards reorders them in every view. Valid rotation bodies can contain up to 2,000 total steps; large workspaces reuse nearby card controls as you navigate. Folded branches intentionally hide their children."] = 2632
-- 76bac84a
T["New / Duplicate / Import / Compare"] = 2633
-- c4875790
T["Choose a category and search for a condition. Hidden removes it from pickers without deleting its definition. Switch Condition controls its availability for automatic rotation switching. Move To stages a category destination; its Apply button confirms the move. The assigned category opens category management. Sidebar arrows and dragging order entries. Page Apply saves the draft; Discard abandons edits to a saved entry. Custom conditions can be edited, duplicated or deleted."] = 2634
-- be63470b
T["Select an effect to edit its name, type and type-specific settings. The icon previews it live. Sequence sections edit animation, color, pulse or custom frames in order. Duplicate creates an independent effect. Drag a sequence card surface to reorder it; fields remain editable. New effects can be configured before naming. Apply saves the draft; Discard abandons edits to a saved entry. Import stages a validated replacement."] = 2635
-- e7df5868
T["Choose an item set and edit its priority list. Global shares the set across profiles. Move arrows change item priority. Bind item set picks up an available item for placement on an action bar; The binding pill removes matching bound bar actions when unbinding, outside combat. Reset restores a packaged set. Search or drag items into reference fields. Apply saves settings; Discard abandons edits to a saved entry. Binding changes are explicit action-bar operations."] = 2636
-- 27a02657
T["Press Enter or leave a text field to stage its value; Apply saves the draft. Invalid text stays red and must be corrected before Apply; Discard can abandon it. Searchable selectors open on click and filter as you type. Section headings collapse or expand their contents."] = 2637
-- 53a70ff7
-- Context: Help topic title at the top of the item list dialog help.
T["Editing this list"] = 2638
-- d71ea291
T["This window edits only the item list you opened. Search or drag items into the fields, then arrange preferred items first. A named item set is shared by its other users; a custom list belongs to the calling condition or action draft. Applying this list does not apply the parent editor."] = 2639
-- 05cdc879
T["Use a row's red trash can to remove that entry from the draft list. This does not delete a named item set or remove an item from your inventory. The removal takes effect when you Apply this list."] = 2640
-- 3cedce54
T["Apply validates every entry and writes the edited list back to its original owner. Discard closes without changing it. Closing with pending edits offers Apply, Discard or Cancel; Cancel keeps this window open. View Changes compares the original list with this draft. If the original list changed elsewhere, close and reopen it before applying."] = 2641
-- 54637cac
T["Proc Glow: use the animated actionbar proc border from LibCustomGlow. Rotation Master checks the required game artwork and animation support before using it. Unsupported clients use Pixel glow instead; the definition remains portable. Color and offsets come from the profile or the cooldown."] = 2642
-- 265e2457
T["Time in seconds for one repeating proc-border animation, from 0.1 to 5. Use the slider or enter an exact value in its number field. Changing the value updates the preview."] = 2643
-- 50bd053e
T["Play the opening burst when this highlight first appears, then repeat its border animation. Off by default. Refreshing an already visible Proc Glow does not restart the burst."] = 2644
-- a0515628
T["Rotations belong to the active settings profile. New copies use Class, shared by your characters of that class; Metadata can change this to This character. Built In rotations show only for their declared class or universal use. Equal identifiers in different owners remain separate entries."] = 2645
-- 774a185e
T["Older rotations without a recorded owner stay in an archive. Recover unassigned rotations opens the current profile and character archives for inspection or copying. Choose Class or This character to adopt one. Adoption preserves its identifier and evidence, refuses an existing destination, and leaves incomplete records unavailable until repaired."] = 2646
-- 4886d663
-- Context: Help topic title in Integrations help for the checkbox that turns on the Questie
--     integration.
T["Enable Questie integration"] = 2647
-- 3a9724aa
T["Review supported addons, detected versions and status by integration type. Expand or collapse each integration group. Click an addon name to choose a copyable release or source link. Configure editor and optional provider preferences here; Apply saves preferences for this profile and Discard keeps saved settings."] = 2648
-- 25f09788
T["Opt in to Questie callbacks for this profile, then Apply. Discard does not change the saved connection. Readiness, API compatibility, source-tested version and native acceptance are reported separately. The adapter retains recent update receipts only; they do not prove quest progress or completion and do not select rotations. No background polling is used."] = 2649
-- 3877e4d7
T["Enable DBM or BigWigs to feed the Boss Mod conditions (encounter, stage and ability timers), then Apply. Only one boss mod can be enabled; enabling one disables the other. RM listens to the boss mod's own callbacks and never polls it or changes its settings. With none enabled, or the enabled addon not loaded, Boss Mod conditions are unavailable. Supported on Classic Era, TBC and Classic progression clients."] = 2650
-- c9949fc6
T["Rotation Master publishes a LibDataBroker data source with the active rotation, a tooltip and click menus. Titan Panel and other LibDataBroker displays show it without further setup: in Titan, add Rotation Master from the plugin menu. Panel absence has no effect on rotation selection."] = 2651
-- 59df493c
T["Record spell cast receipts for thirty seconds without changing settings or gameplay polling. While it runs this button reads Stop cast capture and ends the capture early, keeping what was recorded."] = 2652
-- 0ffbf212
T["Open the copyable cast receipt report. It stays disabled until a cast capture has produced a report and while a capture is running."] = 2653
-- 472590ae
-- Context: Column heading in the addon download links dialog: the website that hosts the download
--     (e.g. CurseForge).
T["Provider"] = 2654
-- e7a241de
-- Context: Column heading in the addon download links dialog: the web address of the download page.
T["URL"] = 2655
-- 8ea4edb6
T["Select URL for copying (Ctrl+C)"] = 2656
-- 42592899
T["Syntax highlighting applies only to the Native Lua editor. Apply saves this preference for the next source-editor opening; it does not switch a selected external editor. Show line numbers under the editor heading applies to every provider."] = 2657
-- eb084da9
T["Enable separately installed Masque here and Apply. General > Preview then provides a Skin dropdown that updates the preview immediately. Masque owns the skin selection; /masque opens its other settings. The preview window keeps its native appearance. Missing or incompatible APIs and provider errors retain the native preview."] = 2658
-- 34199d23
T["Enable Masque in Integrations to choose a skin. Skin changes update the open preview immediately and are saved by Masque, independently of Apply or Discard. Without enabled Masque support, the preview uses Blizzard Classic. Preview toggles sample icons whether Masque is enabled or not."] = 2659
-- 5b167013
T["Click Preview to toggle temporary sample icons when no real recommendations are available. Real recommendations replace the samples. This does not change Preview Spells, cast spells, or save the sample state."] = 2660
-- 04025773
T["Optional conditions use the Announcement condition list and All, Any and Not groups. For spell, pet and item announcements, they run when the configured action and event match. For Via Script/Macro, they run when you invoke the saved identifier. Each output card checks its own conditions. Only a matching result allows that output; unavailable data skips that card while later cards remain independent. In Group can check the Spell recipient recorded for this cast, including click casting, without using your selected target. Choose Announcement target to check the spell recipient for automatic entries, or the supplied unit for Via Script/Macro; Whisper uses that same supplied unit. Automatic entries pass the recorded recipient name to native unit queries. A missing or unresolvable recipient skips its required condition; an unrelated selected target is never substituted. Missing or ambiguous required recipients do not match. Apply in the condition editor updates the announcement draft; Apply on Announces saves it. Cancel or Discard abandons draft changes."] = 2661
-- 6c64ce13
T["Choose the unit whose membership in your party or raid is checked. Player keeps the original player group-status behavior. Spell recipient uses only the current announcement event context; without that readable context the result is unavailable. It never substitutes your selected target or a previous cast."] = 2662
-- 27cc3255
T["Checked tests raid membership only. Unchecked tests party membership or raid membership. A known nonmember is false; unavailable native data stays unavailable, including under NOT."] = 2663
-- d44133b4
T["Choose tabs to browse Rotations, General, Conditions, Functions, Effects, Item Sets, Announces, Profiles and Integrations. The opened panes have their own Help for page controls. Search and filters belong to the current page. Built In entries remain read-only; Duplicate creates an editable copy."] = 2664
-- 28510b80
T["Scale changes the whole workbench and its child windows from 70% to 130%. Drag the top-left slider or enter an integer percentage and press Enter. Escape restores the saved scale text. Drag the title bar to move; drag the lower-right corner to resize."] = 2665
-- 81701f02
T["Close with X, Escape, or right-click inside the frontmost RM window. Child dialogs have their own close controls and follow the window scale. The language selector changes the workbench language; project links open a copyable address."] = 2666
-- ae7a65d1
T["Most settings and source editors keep drafts until Apply. Leaving a dirty page offers Apply, Discard or Cancel; invalid fields remain visible. Profile activation and confirmed replacement, action-bar binding and diagnostic capture have their own explicit actions. Help never applies or discards edits."] = 2667
-- 2d6b5cc8
T["Gold question marks open full Help for their window, page or card. Hover controls for brief tips. Help does not save settings or commit pending text; spell and item fields keep their native reference tooltips."] = 2668
-- 8fb57308
T["Open full Help for these controls without applying edits."] = 2669
-- b9cc9038
T["Explain window navigation, scaling, closing and drafts."] = 2670
-- 859a4f2c
T["Open full Help for this page without switching tabs or applying edits."] = 2671
-- c0a96039
T["Set the workbench and child-window scale from 70% to 130%; enter a whole percentage or drag the slider."] = 2672
-- 36760759
T["Edit the value; Enter or leaving the field checks and accepts valid text. Page Help explains when changes are saved."] = 2673
-- 43f47d2a
T["Click to toggle this option. Page Help explains when changes are saved."] = 2674
-- 1b2d4c57
T["Use this control for the current page; page Help explains its options and consequences."] = 2675
-- d885c6a2
T["Help for this condition is unavailable. Its registered definition is missing, disabled or waiting for required functions. Opening Help does not register pending or imported source."] = 2676
-- 711bb065
T["This registered condition does not provide Help."] = 2677
-- d9c613e5
T["Open Help for this condition without changing its fields."] = 2678
-- ac330ed0
T["Select all export text for manual copying. This button does not send it anywhere."] = 2679
-- d8332c9a
T["Clear the transfer text. A previous preview becomes invalid; saved settings stay unchanged."] = 2680
-- 7b980fdf
T["Import into the displayed destination. Read the destination and review requirements before continuing."] = 2681
-- f71901b9
T["Close this dialog without importing its text."] = 2682
-- 536a00ad
T["Choose a new named copy or replacement of the selected editable entry."] = 2683
-- 28928c04
T["Set the name for a new copy. Replacement keeps the selected entry as its destination."] = 2684
-- 128c10d4
T["Preview import shows everything this import contains, read-only, the way the editor shows it. Nothing is saved."] = 2685
-- 853ec82f
T["Check import lists problems with the text instead of its content: why it cannot be imported and any unsupported data. It does not import or change anything."] = 2686
-- 27a3bd58
T["Explain profile import destinations and when changes are saved."] = 2687
-- ca00de4c
T["Copy the text to export a profile, or paste profile text to import. The destination controls choose a new profile or replacement of the selected saved profile. Opening Help does not decode, import, or apply the text."] = 2688
-- 2625de29
T["REPLACE applies immediately to the selected saved profile after Import. Replacing the active profile resets it and applies the imported settings; replacing another profile writes that profile. Reopen the import if the selected saved profile changes."] = 2689
-- 74cf2bda
T["NEW stages the imported profile in the Profiles editor. Import fills a new-profile draft; the new profile is not saved or activated until you complete the creation controls in that editor. Give it an unused name."] = 2690
-- 00c3d8f9
T["Explain this read-only review of imported source."] = 2691
-- 3b8fed45
T["This view shows the selected imported function or condition source, its original and destination identifiers, and available metadata. For a condition, choose a callback to inspect its text. This view and its Help do not compile, execute, accept, or register the source. Return to the bundle review to decide whether to import it."] = 2692
-- c60faea8
T["Close this read-only source view and return to the bundle review."] = 2693
-- 49411dfb
T["Validate the pasted bundle and build a proposed import plan. Review does not apply the plan."] = 2694
-- b8726351
T["Include referenced custom function dependencies when producing export text."] = 2695
-- 74de20bd
T["Explain dependency-bundle export, review, and explicit import."] = 2696
-- 4449aeeb
T["Export produces a function or condition bundle, optionally with its custom function dependencies. For import, paste bundle text, choose Review import, inspect the proposed identifiers and conflicts, and review source before applying. Apply import can register trusted Lua source; accept only source you intend to run. Changing the text invalidates the prior plan. Opening Help neither reviews nor applies the bundle."] = 2697
-- 067adc87
T["Explain rotation preview, destination, and import scope."] = 2698
-- fe3fd231
T["Copy the text to export the current rotation, or paste a rotation to import. Choose replacement of the selected editable rotation or a new named copy. Class and This character set the owner of a new copy; replacement keeps the original owner. The imported rotation is opened for editing after a successful import."] = 2699
-- d6789183
T["With Replace selected entry ticked, the button reads Compare import and shows what would change in that rotation. For a new named copy it reads Preview import and shows everything the import contains, read-only, as the rotation editor shows it. Neither saves anything. Import is enabled only for a ready preview or comparison; changing the text requires another one. Check import shows read-only diagnostics, including unsupported data that prevents import."] = 2700
-- 9a2297f1
T["Explain this read-only incoming rotation comparison."] = 2701
-- 4f0c847b
T["This view compares the saved or exported rotation with the current incoming preview. It does not apply changes. Close it to choose the destination and import from the transfer dialog. A changed preview, closed owner, or changed profile retires this comparison Help."] = 2702
-- c091ac0b
T["Compare import shows what would change in the entry you are replacing, side by side with its current content. Nothing is saved."] = 2703
-- 64144a9e
T["Explain this read-only preview of the incoming rotation."] = 2704
-- 91ca45b8
T["This view shows the rotation as it would be imported: name, specializations, switch condition, steps and cooldowns. It is read-only and works on a copy; it saves and changes nothing. Close it to choose the destination and import from the transfer dialog. A changed text, closed transfer or changed profile retires this Help."] = 2705
-- 5ac254c6
-- Context: Help topic title in the Announces help: an example of how a macro calls an announcement.
T["Macro invocation"] = 2706
-- 94a47c93
-- Context: Help topic title in the Announces help: the unit that a macro passes to the
--     announcement.
T["Supplied macro unit"] = 2707
-- c3039a0d
T["Invoke this saved identifier directly from your macro. The supplied unit controls Announcement target conditions and Whisper; there is no implicit target."] = 2708
-- d4f140f6
T["Via Script/Macro is invoked by its saved Identifier rather than a cast event. It does not require a stored spell or item. Current conditions must match before any output. This call attempts output synchronously; it does not establish that a spell was cast or succeeded."] = 2709
-- 978b4fbf
T["Use a unique, case-sensitive identifier of at most 64 ASCII characters. Start with a letter or underscore; subsequent characters may also include digits, dots or hyphens. Identifiers are scoped to the active profile, including disabled entries. Duplicate assigns a distinct identifier; ambiguous imports and Apply are rejected."] = 2710
-- 7247934f
T["Use /run RM_Annouce('FOO','mouseover',nil). RM_Announce is the same function. The target unit and spell are optional: /run RM_Announce('FOO',nil,403) or /run RM_Announce('FOO','target','Lightning Bolt'). Spell names depend on client language. {{event}} becomes Via Script/Macro; {{target}} and {{spell}} use the supplied arguments. A required missing argument skips output. {{item}} is not supplied by this API. A resurrection message announces an attempt, not a completed resurrection. Examples are text only; RM does not create or execute macros."] = 2711
-- fda702d4
T["Supply a readable unit token such as mouseover, target or focus. RM resolves that exact unit name and rechecks its identity during delivery. Announcement target conditions and Whisper use this same unit. Omitting the argument does not use your selected target, yourself, a prior cast or a prior macro call. Missing Announcement target data remains unavailable, including under NOT."] = 2712
-- 4c48bcf5
T["Checked directs a named emote to the supplied macro unit. Missing or unreadable target data skips the targeted emote; unchecked is targetless."] = 2713
-- 4dbc9c41
T["Available only for Via Script/Macro. Attempt a Say message directly in the invoking call. Blizzard may reject macro-origin chat, including during instance encounters; RM does not attest hardware input, defer delivery, retry or guarantee visible output."] = 2714
-- a1cf5fb0
T["Available only for Via Script/Macro. Attempt a Yell message directly in the invoking call. Native macro and encounter restrictions still apply; a completed API call is not confirmation of delivery."] = 2715
-- a736bec3
T["Available only for Via Script/Macro. Whisper uses the exact supplied unit name and requires a readable player identity. No target means no Whisper. Native macro and encounter restrictions still apply; RM never substitutes another recipient or retries."] = 2716
-- b6082c37
T["Offer this condition type when editing announcement conditions. This flag is independent of Switch Condition and does not remove or invalidate conditions already saved in announcements."] = 2717
-- 45320409
T["One trigger can send an ordered series of outputs. Each expanded card has its own destination, text or sound, conditions and enabled state. Help describes that card. Duplicate makes an independent card; delete removes it. Use the arrows, or drag a card from anywhere on it, to change order. Add output, on the Outputs header row, appends a card; drag it into a gap to insert one there. A legacy announcement stays unchanged on display. Adding, duplicating or removing a card, choosing Channel, or changing to an action type that cannot use its saved destination converts only the draft to output cards. Up to 64 outputs are allowed; an empty series sends nothing. Apply saves the draft and Discard restores it."] = 2718
-- 3c9708b1
T["Via Script/Macro outputs can send to a joined chat channel. Open Channel to refresh the joined names, then select the exact name. A saved name remains visible when unavailable; that output is skipped until the channel is joined under that name. Numeric channel IDs are not saved and channels are never joined automatically. Native delivery permissions still apply."] = 2719
-- 6de77638
T["Choose an announcement trigger, then edit its always expanded output cards. Each card has a destination, conditions, enabled state and Help. Add, duplicate, delete, move or drag outputs within the announcement. Joined channel names are available for Via Script/Macro. New opens a draft; Apply saves it and Discard restores it. Imports are validated and never execute code."] = 2720
-- 318a2558
T["Recommends whatever spell Blizzard's Assisted Combat suggests next, read each time the rotation is evaluated. It highlights that spell's button and shows in the preview like a spell step, and is held to the same requirements: known, usable, off cooldown and in range. When nothing is suggested, the suggested spell is not on your bars, or Assisted Combat is unavailable (anywhere but Retail, or a specialization without it), the step is skipped. Rotation list only."] = 2721
-- d462cf8d
T["Who highlights the button while a \"Blizzard's suggestion\" step is the recommendation. Rotation Master's glow uses the effect below. Blizzard's Assisted Highlight turns on the game's own highlight (Options, Gameplay, Combat, Assisted Highlight) while a rotation with that step is active, and Rotation Master leaves that step's button to it; Both shows the two. Rotation Master turns Blizzard's highlight on only outside combat, never changes it if it was already on, and puts your setting back when the rotation ends, Rotation Master is disabled, or you log out or reload. If you change the setting yourself meanwhile, your choice is kept. Blizzard's highlight follows Blizzard's suggestion all the time, also while another step is recommended, and it shows on Blizzard's own action bars only, so choose Rotation Master's glow or Both with a bar addon. The choice is hidden on clients without Blizzard's highlight (Forever and the Classic clients)."] = 2722
-- e031d376
T["Add Rotation Master lines to spell and item tooltips. This is the master switch: off, Rotation Master adds nothing to any tooltip, and the options below do nothing. Lines are only added, never read from the tooltip, so other tooltip addons are unaffected."] = 2723
-- b52dc56f
T["In an item tooltip, list the Rotation Master item sets that contain the item: your profile's and the shared ones from the Item Sets page. Names beyond the limit below end the line with how many more there are."] = 2724
-- a142e568
T["In a spell or item tooltip, list the rotations for your current specialization that use it as a step in the rotation or cooldown list. A rotation that is switched off is shown dimmed and marked disabled. Built In rotations that are not for this version of the game or your specialization are left out. The list is refreshed out of combat after a rotation or item set changes."] = 2725
-- 5e8b512d
T["Also count a spell or item that appears only inside a condition (for example \"spell is ready\" or \"item is carried\"), not just as a step. Off by default because it lists more rotations."] = 2726
-- dffd6006
T["How many names a tooltip line lists before it ends with \"(+N more)\". A lower number keeps tooltips short."] = 2727
-- 83e079d3
T["Your talent specialization. Choose a class, then one of its specializations; your own class is selected first, and other classes are offered for rotations shared between characters. A specialization of another class is always false."] = 2728
-- a449bf6b
T["Retail and Mists of Pandaria Classic compare your active specialization. Classic Era, Burning Crusade and Wrath compare your primary talent tree, the one tree with the most points; Feral and Guardian both mean Feral Combat there. Forever cannot tell its specializations apart this way. No specialization yet, tied or unspent trees and unreadable values are unavailable, including under NOT. The answer is cached until your talents or specialization change."] = 2729
-- 86569ac1
T["What is equipped in the main hand, off hand or ranged slot: nothing, any weapon, a one-handed, two-handed or ranged weapon, a shield, an off-hand item, or one weapon type such as Daggers. Types are read from the item's class and subclass, so they work in every language. The answer is cached until your equipment changes."] = 2730
-- 96a5754f
T["Dual wielding: off hand holds any weapon. Titan's Grip: off hand holds a two-handed weapon. Backstab and Ambush: main hand holds Daggers. Shield Slam or a tank set: off hand holds a shield. The ranged slot exists only before Mists of Pandaria; elsewhere, and while item data is still loading, this condition is unavailable, including under NOT."] = 2731
-- 0e0d00b2
T["Not on your action bars"] = 2732
-- c8117094
T["An amber border and warning mark a card whose action no action bar button holds right now. Rotation Master highlights an action by lighting the button that holds it, so that step is skipped (a cooldown is never shown) until you put it on a bar. The warning updates when your bars change. Red still marks invalid data."] = 2733
-- 2c7e6247
T["Actions must also be on an action bar: Rotation Master highlights an action by lighting the button that holds it, so a step or cooldown that no button holds is skipped, and its card shows an amber warning."] = 2734
-- cc011249
T["Matches while the game says a boss encounter is in progress. Unlike the Boss Mod Encounter condition it needs no boss mod, and it knows nothing of which boss or stage it is. It starts when the encounter starts and ends on a kill, a wipe or a reset. It reads in combat on every edition, Retail and Forever included."] = 2735
-- bec26f34
T["The level of the Mythic+ keystone you are running. It is 0 whenever you are not in a Mythic+ dungeon, so 'at least 10' is only true inside a run of that level. Retail only."] = 2736
-- a4530fa7
T["The hero talent tree you have chosen. Pick a tree from the list, which shows the trees of the rotation's specialization, or choose 'Any hero talent tree' to match once you have chosen one. A tree can also be entered by its ID, to share a rotation with another class. Below the level that offers hero talents, or before you pick a tree, no tree is chosen. Retail only."] = 2737
-- 88cf82f7
T["Matches while the game shows the activation glow on this spell, the golden border an action button gets when a proc makes the spell castable or stronger. It asks the game directly, so it still reads when the buff behind the proc is hidden from addons in combat. Choose the spell as it appears on your bars; its base and override forms are checked too. Unavailable, never simply false, if the game cannot answer."] = 2738
-- c9e6ec28
T["How happy your Hunter pet is: Unhappy, Content or Happy, as the game reports it. No pet, or a pet that is not a Hunter pet, is in none of these moods. Classic Era, Burning Crusade and Wrath only."] = 2739
-- d6742b74
T["The damage waiting in your Brewmaster Monk's Stagger pool, or, with the box ticked, that damage as a percent of your maximum health. Mists of Pandaria, Retail and Forever only. On Retail and Forever the game can hide the pool from addons in combat, and always hides maximum health, so the percent form is unavailable there and the amount is unavailable whenever the game hides it; neither is ever guessed."] = 2740
-- 22cccaf0
T["Advise a spell even when you do not have the mana or other resource for it right now. Without this, a spell you cannot afford is skipped like any other step that is not ready. The spell must still be learned, off cooldown and usable for another reason, and its conditions still apply."] = 2741
-- 1bf91ced
T["Retail and Forever can hide whether a spell is usable from addons in some situations. The spell is then skipped whether or not this option is on."] = 2742
-- 0c4bd263
T["Advise a spell or item even when your target is out of its range. Without this, a step whose range check fails is skipped. The spell or item must still be learned or owned, off cooldown and usable, and its conditions still apply."] = 2743
-- cb691e6c
T["Adopt several at once"] = 2744
-- 6ac62581
T["Adopt all and Adopt all from specialization adopt every listed record in one step, for the owner chosen under Applies to. Each record is adopted on its own, exactly as a single adoption would be: a record whose destination already exists, or that is incomplete, stays in the archive and is named in the result."] = 2745
